      "writtenOn": "2024-04-22T16:38:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The obvious question here is: from an API perspective, how should the caller enable this chain?\n\nIt looks like currently this chain is enabled/disabled by NPMS (which will also be the caller of the methods to add/remove UIDs from this chain) by calling INetd\u0027s set bandwidthSetInterfaceQuota method. If there is no quota to set, then it passes down QUOTA_UNLIMITED.\n\nLong term it would be nice if:\n1. NPMS only calls INetd.bandwidthSetInterfaceQuota if there is actually a quota on the interface\n2. This \"chain\" is not enabled/disabled inside netd but is automatically enabled on metered networks.\n3. NPMS sets interface quotas by calling ConnectivityManager APIs instead of calling into netd.\n\nI don\u0027t think this is something we can do in V because #3 will need an API change, but can you file a bug for this? I think it\u0027s similar to what Jimi, Patrick and Maciej are working on, so maybe coordinate with them.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1080,
        "startChar": 59,
        "endLine": 1080,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "49506f14cbf258d95d25f20e552800944ff17acb",
